{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/thm-grobner-shirshov-basis-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:grobner-shirshov-basis-exists","kind":"theorem","title":"Existence of Groebner--Shirshov basis","uses":["papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-non-commutative-formal-group","papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-grobner-shirshov-basis"],"cites":["references/fred2005"],"tags":["groebner-shirshov","existence","flat-deformation"],"leanRef":"fred2005:Fred2005.grobner_shirshov_basis_exists","text":"grobner-shirshov-basis-exists.md","leanSource":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/grobner-shirshov-basis-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:grobner-shirshov-basis-exists\"></a><p>The <a href=\"#def:grobner-shirshov-basis\">Groebner--Shirshov basis</a> for\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Dist}(G)</code> exists and yields a flat deformation of\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Dist}(H)</code>.  The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Serre relations form a Groebner--Shirshov\nsystem whose composition lemma (confluence) holds.</p>\n<p>Reference: <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"fred2005\">[fred2005]</span>, Proposition 3.8 and Theorem 3.15.</p>\n","source":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/grobner-shirshov-basis-exists.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"1.4.2"}
